// Copyright (c) 2026 Capital41 | MIT License
// CAPITAL41 CRYPTO PERP STRESS

// What it does:
// - Detects crypto-specific stress using perp basis, OI impulse, and
//   liquidation wick behavior.
// - Flags long-squeeze risk, short-squeeze risk, cascade starts, and reset
//   completion.
// - Includes weekend sensitivity controls for 24/7 markets.
//
// TradingView setup:
// 1) Open TradingView -> Pine Editor.
// 2) Paste this script, Save, and Add to chart.
// 3) Use intraday or 4h on liquid perp pairs.
// 4) Set Spot/Perp/OI symbols for your exchange.
//
// Usage guide:
// - Long-squeeze risk: crowded longs + OI build + downside liquidation wick.
// - Short-squeeze risk: crowded shorts + OI build + upside liquidation wick.
// - Cascade tags: stress + break of prior bar extreme.
// - Reset complete: basis normalizes, OI flushes, and volatility compresses.

- a configurable opening range and trading session;
- confirmed local-bar breakouts;
- fast/slow EMA, DMI/ADX, and confirmed higher-timeframe EMA filters;
- ATR-derived stops and equity-risk position sizing;
- two 50% take-profit orders;
- maximum daily loss, maximum drawdown, and daily trade limits;
- optional flattening when the trading session ends;
- an on-chart status dashboard.

- confirmed 4H EMA bias and expansion/pullback state;
- the latest confirmed three-candle 4H fair value gap;
- a 15m FVG touch, liquidity sweep, and MSS or CISD confirmation;
- a retrace into the confirmed 15m FVG;
- a 1m liquidity sweep followed by a 1m FVG and MSS/CISD break;
- a sweep-based stop and opposing 15m liquidity target with an R fallback.
